0..77 Comment "// A flow between types whose written endpoints disagree with its translator:"
78..154 Comment "// `A ⇝ B` abbreviates `Flow[.A = Type](A, B)`, and `Flow.into` introduces"
155..167 Comment "// it at the"
168..245 Comment "// translator\'s own domain and codomain, so the relation written backwards is"
246..294 Comment "// refused where the flow is checked against it."
